## Part C - EXPLAIN ANALYZE per query path (Step 2 - done)

Method: `p101_explain.py` runs the real service/view querysets (feed/services.py, search/services.py, content public lists, moderation queue list, stories public list) with a Django `execute_wrapper` to capture the exact SQL, then `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` on each (one warm-up run, one recorded run). Each is re-planned with `SET enable_seqscan = off` (diagnostic only, reset afterwards): if the planner then picks an index, the index is USABLE for that query shape and the seq scan was a cost-based choice; if it still cannot, the shape does not fit any index.

Fixture: `P101|FIXTURE|customer=p101_cust_0|follows=24|category_id=11|busy_business=12|story_business=63`

Verdict column is automatic (index names found in the plan). Human interpretation and fixes are in Part E (Step 3).

